  "worked_solution": "Isolating the sixth-degree term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x-2)^{6}-1 & \\ge 3 \\\\ 2(x-2)^{6} & \\ge 4 \\\\ (x-2)^{6} & \\ge 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take the sixth root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[6]{(x-2)^{6}} & \\ge \\sqrt[6]{2} \\\\ |x-2| & \\ge \\sqrt[6]{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\nx-2\\le -\\sqrt[6]{2}\\,\\text{or}\\,x-2\\ge \\sqrt[6]{2}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is\n\n$$\nx\\le 2-\\sqrt[6]{2}\\,\\text{or}\\,x\\ge 2+\\sqrt[6]{2}.\n$$",
